[]   4) What is this Elbereth thing that everyone talks about?

the difference between a great game and a quick death. `Elbereth' (from
J.R.R. Tolkien) is engraved on the ground (`E' command) with your fingers
(`-') or with an instrument of your choosing from your inventory. the
engraving can be "in the dust" or "in the rock". bladed weapons will
become dull in the process of engraving in the rock with the exception
of athames. certain wands also engrave in the rock. engravings in the
rock are somewhat more durable than those in the dust but either type
has the same problem. engravings in the dust can be easily erased and
written again. the problem with engraving `Elbereth' is that it is only
effective while the engraving is intact! the engraving may become smudged
when you "act" while standing on the engraving. you can, of course, rise
above this problem with appropriate magic!! the effect of standing over
an intact engraving of `Elbereth' is to cause monsters (nearly all non-@'s)
that would normally try to attack you to turn away for a while instead.
while the monsters won't attack in this situation they may still use
missile weapons on you. you should periodically look (`:' command) to
see that your engraving is still intact. either that or the monsters
will take the oppurtunity to remind you. the strategy is really a
defensive one, you should prepare to use it before it is too late ...

[]   5) ... how do you discover what kinds of potions or scrolls you
[]      have without using identify scrolls?

identify spells from spellbooks and opulant thrones are generally on
par with blessed scrolls of identify (i.e. multiple identifies).

you have to read scrolls (strategically) to identify them. they say that
monsters will not walk on scare monster scrolls ...

when quaffing from sinks you will occasionally sip a stream of colored
liquid whose effect will correspond to the effect of the same potion,
but you could get toxic waste and undergo a freakish metamorphosis. be
prepared, turning into a large monster has predictable results (which
cannot be reversed!). polymorphing can be controlled to an extent and
is only scary the first time (until you get killed or something ...).

you didn't ask ... pay attention to the feelings you may get when eating
monster corpses. these generally correspond to the acquisition of valuable
intrinsic attributes like poison resistance ("you feel healthy") which
you'll want to acquire asap ...

